WEBVTT

00:01:52.609 --> 00:01:54.338
Halt!

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:56.401
We are in a state of war,
so no one is allowed...

00:01:56.479 --> 00:01:58.311
...into Valis territory under
any circumstances!

00:01:58.381 --> 00:02:00.213
What kinda attitude is that...?!

00:02:02.318 --> 00:02:03.752
Hold it, Garrack.

00:02:03.820 --> 00:02:06.755
We're messengers
from the kingdom of Flaim.

00:02:06.823 --> 00:02:09.121
We ask permission
to enter your domain.

00:02:09.192 --> 00:02:12.423
From Flaim...? I beg your pardon!

00:02:15.231 --> 00:02:19.964
| understand the need for security,
but is Valis really this bad off?

00:02:20.036 --> 00:02:21.936
Yeah, things aren't looking good.

00:02:22.005 --> 00:02:24.235
We've taken a lot of damage
from the Marmo forces.

00:02:24.307 --> 00:02:27.538
Would this dispatch be about Flaim
sending reinforcements here?!

00:02:28.912 --> 00:02:31.882
Is King Kashue coming to save Valis?

00:02:31.948 --> 00:02:33.746
When do the reinforcements arrive?

00:02:33.816 --> 00:02:36.012
Soldiers of the Valis forces
need help...

00:02:36.085 --> 00:02:37.985
...from other kingdoms this badly?!

00:02:58.441 --> 00:03:00.102
It's quiet, isn't it,
Priest Greevus?

00:03:00.176 --> 00:03:04.238
Yes, very. People must be
frightened of war with the Marmo.

00:03:04.681 --> 00:03:07.013
Probably.
Those soldiers at the fortress...

00:03:07.083 --> 00:03:11.020
...said the Valis forces were
having a really rough time.

00:03:11.087 --> 00:03:15.684
So they're counting on Flaim's
king for help. Not a good sign.

00:03:15.758 --> 00:03:19.160
King Etoh has a good
reputation, doesn't he?

00:03:19.228 --> 00:03:22.823
Do you think his people
have lost faith in him?

00:03:23.433 --> 00:03:25.299
No, that's not it.

00:03:25.368 --> 00:03:28.736
Besides being the best friend
of Parn, the free knight...

00:03:28.805 --> 00:03:31.399
...he's also the high priest
of the temple of Falis.

00:03:31.474 --> 00:03:35.001
But people usually look
for heroes in times of war.

00:03:35.078 --> 00:03:39.811
And the people suited to being
heroes aren't priests or wizards.

00:03:40.216 --> 00:03:41.809
Only warriors.

00:03:43.052 --> 00:03:44.884
Warriors, huh...?

00:03:52.695 --> 00:03:54.754
Is this the royal
palace of Valis?

00:03:54.831 --> 00:03:56.993
The holy palace.

00:03:59.268 --> 00:04:01.566
We've come from
the kingdom of Flaim...

00:04:01.638 --> 00:04:03.970
...with a dispatch
by order of King Kashue.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.532
| request an
audience with King Etoh.

00:04:06.809 --> 00:04:08.299
We appreciate your arrival.

00:04:08.378 --> 00:04:11.678
Messengers from Flaim have arrived!
Lower the drawbridge!

00:04:28.264 --> 00:04:31.529
Garrack, you've been jumpy
for a while now. What's wrong?

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:35.196
N- Nothing.
I'm just tense for some reason.

00:04:35.271 --> 00:04:37.535
Guilty conscience, maybe?

00:04:37.607 --> 00:04:40.599
Wh- What do you mean?!
I haven't done anything!

00:04:40.677 --> 00:04:42.668
What's got you so angry now?

00:04:42.745 --> 00:04:45.407
'Cuz you're talking
crap to me, Leaf!

00:04:45.481 --> 00:04:46.846
Would you both just shut up?!

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.594
I've brought the messengers!

00:05:32.695 --> 00:05:36.290
| am Spark, knight
in training from Flaim.

00:05:36.365 --> 00:05:39.824
| welcome you from your long
journey, messengers from Flaim.

00:05:40.236 --> 00:05:42.967
Do you have a message for me?

00:05:43.039 --> 00:05:44.234
Yes.

00:05:58.821 --> 00:06:02.883
I have read King Kashue's
message to me.

00:06:02.959 --> 00:06:05.121
Be sure to store this carefully.

00:06:05.461 --> 00:06:08.954
Master Spark, are you aware
of the dispatch's contents?

00:06:09.031 --> 00:06:12.092
No, Highness, I'm not.
What is it?

00:06:12.168 --> 00:06:17.868
Nothing serious, but there was
a message in it for you.

00:06:18.674 --> 00:06:21.234
Wh- What sort of message, Highness?

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:23.642
Before I tell you, I want
to ask you something.

00:06:23.713 --> 00:06:27.115
Were you able to recover
the stolen treasure?

00:06:27.183 --> 00:06:30.209
N- No, Highness. We took
care of the thieves...

00:06:30.286 --> 00:06:32.983
...but they'd already passed
it on to someone else.

00:06:33.055 --> 00:06:35.217
We're still looking for it.

00:06:35.792 --> 00:06:37.317
| see...

00:06:37.393 --> 00:06:40.158
| was wondering
if you would allow us...

00:06:40.229 --> 00:06:42.630
...to search the area
inside Valis, Your Highness.

00:06:42.698 --> 00:06:44.166
That won't be necessary.

00:06:44.233 --> 00:06:45.894
What do you mean, Highness?

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:48.562
According to this message,
if you have not recovered...

00:06:48.638 --> 00:06:51.198
...the treasure when I receive it...

00:06:51.274 --> 00:06:54.471
...King Kashue orders that you're
to return to Flaim immediately.

00:06:56.279 --> 00:06:58.077
King Etoh, is that true?!

00:06:59.282 --> 00:07:01.376
-I don't believe it!
- What is he doing?!

00:07:02.618 --> 00:07:04.484
Forgive me, Highness.
That was rude of me.

00:07:05.788 --> 00:07:07.586
How could I say that?!

00:07:07.657 --> 00:07:10.820
King Etoh's a priest!
He wouldn't lie to me!

00:07:10.893 --> 00:07:12.452
And besides that...!

00:07:12.528 --> 00:07:15.793
That was definitely the
message from King Kashue.

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.659
There goes any chance
I have of completing my mission!

00:07:25.975 --> 00:07:29.605
Didn't King Kashue have
any hopes for me at all?!

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:34.114
He probably never expected me
to be able to recover the treasure!

00:07:34.183 --> 00:07:36.208
That's why he sent that message!

00:07:36.285 --> 00:07:38.447
King Kashue probably thought
it would be too dangerous...

00:07:38.521 --> 00:07:41.286
...for you to go searching Valis
for the treasure during wartime.

00:07:41.357 --> 00:07:44.816
Exactly. His Highness just
wants to protect his people.

00:07:44.894 --> 00:07:51.357
But... If we don't recover the Soul
Crystal Ball, then Neese will be...!

00:07:51.434 --> 00:07:55.496
It's all right. The other implement,
the Staff of Life...

00:07:55.571 --> 00:07:58.905
...is being guarded here in Valis
in the temple of Falis.

00:07:58.975 --> 00:08:01.137
Will the Staff of Life be safe?

00:08:01.210 --> 00:08:03.201
Yes, I think so.

00:08:04.413 --> 00:08:05.744
Really...

00:08:05.815 --> 00:08:09.149
Still, it's kind of a let-down after
we make it all the way to Valis.

00:08:09.218 --> 00:08:12.188
Yeah, right. I still think
the bag man's going to...

00:08:12.255 --> 00:08:15.088
...take a ship from Roid to
get the crystal to Kanon.

00:08:16.292 --> 00:08:19.592
Captain, should we just follow
King Kashue's orders and go home?

00:08:19.662 --> 00:08:20.993
No, but...

00:08:21.063 --> 00:08:23.088
Or are you going to up
and disobey his orders?

00:08:23.165 --> 00:08:24.633
Whoa! Whoa!

00:08:24.700 --> 00:08:27.931
Excuse me.
This may not be a solution...

00:08:28.004 --> 00:08:30.837
...but we've been invited
to a banquet tonight.

00:08:30.907 --> 00:08:33.001
We still have some
time until sunset...

00:08:33.075 --> 00:08:36.534
...50 I suggest we ask to do little
sightseeing down by the docks.

00:08:36.612 --> 00:08:38.706
Oh, really? And do what?

00:08:38.781 --> 00:08:41.148
We'll investigate the port of Roid.

00:08:41.217 --> 00:08:45.984
Then, if we find a clue, we can
think over what to do next.

00:08:46.055 --> 00:08:47.921
You sorcerers
really ARE pretty smart!

00:08:49.392 --> 00:08:53.226
Wh- What do you think,
Priest Greevus?

00:08:53.296 --> 00:08:56.266
| don't approve of
deliberate lying...

00:08:56.332 --> 00:09:00.291
...but my god Myrii can overlook
such a small sin in this case.

00:09:00.536 --> 00:09:02.436
All right, then! It's settled!

00:09:02.505 --> 00:09:04.166
Are you coming to the
port with us, Neese?

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:09.144
I'm sorry, but I thought
I'd visit with King Etoh.

00:09:09.612 --> 00:09:13.879
King Etoh is an old friend
of Lady Neese's family.

00:09:15.918 --> 00:09:17.113
| see...

00:09:17.186 --> 00:09:19.120
Well, that just leaves...

00:09:19.188 --> 00:09:21.680
...getting an opinion
from our captain.

00:09:22.124 --> 00:09:23.717
What'll we do, Spark?

00:09:23.793 --> 00:09:25.955
Let's go, Captain!

00:09:32.601 --> 00:09:36.401
All right, fine.
We've come this far, anyway.

00:09:36.472 --> 00:09:38.497
Let's do all that we can!

00:09:38.574 --> 00:09:40.906
Okay, it's settled!
Let's go, everyone!

00:09:40.977 --> 00:09:42.706
| don't wanna hear
YOU giving ME orders!

00:09:42.778 --> 00:09:44.473
Oh, shut up!

00:09:49.118 --> 00:09:53.021
80, which ships are
suspicious and which aren't?

00:09:54.824 --> 00:09:57.555
We're just going to have
to check out each one.

00:09:57.626 --> 00:10:02.723
But if we do this too openly,
King Etoh may hear about it.

00:10:03.733 --> 00:10:08.034
C'mon, Captain. Have you decided
what we're going to do yet?

00:10:09.839 --> 00:10:13.298
| wish Neese was here
with us to help out on this.

00:10:13.376 --> 00:10:16.437
Now come on, all of you!
Why are you so depressed?

00:10:16.512 --> 00:10:17.570
Ryna...

00:10:17.646 --> 00:10:21.105
At a time like this, you go to
where there's lots of people.

00:10:21.183 --> 00:10:22.844
Go there for what?

00:10:22.918 --> 00:10:26.718
We just let it slip that we're
looking for a ship to Kanon.

00:10:27.089 --> 00:10:30.457
Then we let our rumor
find the ship for us.

00:10:31.127 --> 00:10:31.992
I get you...

00:10:32.061 --> 00:10:34.120
Well, then, where do we go?

00:10:34.196 --> 00:10:36.756
How about a place where
there's lots of sailors?

00:10:38.934 --> 00:10:40.925
Of course! A tavern!

00:10:59.221 --> 00:11:00.848
Uh, excuse me...

00:11:00.923 --> 00:11:02.118
What's up?

00:11:02.191 --> 00:11:04.922
We didn't just
come here to eat, right?

00:11:04.994 --> 00:11:08.487
Yeah, right. Okay, Captain,
start spreading our rumor.

00:11:08.564 --> 00:11:10.589
I'm eating as fast as I can.

00:11:13.235 --> 00:11:14.760
Could you please not laugh?

00:11:14.837 --> 00:11:17.204
Guess it's up to me.

00:11:25.481 --> 00:11:27.950
Keep your hands to yourself, pal!

00:11:32.688 --> 00:11:35.214
Gimme a drink for this.

00:11:35.291 --> 00:11:37.726
Y- You wanna use
this gem for that?!

00:11:37.793 --> 00:11:40.387
Use whatever's left over to buy
around for everyone in here.

00:11:42.164 --> 00:11:44.758
Looks like business
is pretty good for you.

00:11:44.834 --> 00:11:46.359
Well, there's a reason for that.

00:11:47.303 --> 00:11:50.102
Is there a
ship bound for Kanon?

00:11:50.172 --> 00:11:51.970
If there is, I want
to book passage on it.

00:11:52.041 --> 00:11:54.135
Kanon's an enemy country!

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:57.236
No goods or people are
allowed to be shipped there.

00:11:57.313 --> 00:12:00.339
If the guards find out,
you'll be arrested.

00:12:00.416 --> 00:12:02.180
I told you I had a reason.

00:12:02.251 --> 00:12:05.221
My friends and I want to become
mercenaries for the Marmo.

00:12:05.287 --> 00:12:08.655
Mercenaries for the Marmo?!

00:12:09.191 --> 00:12:11.922
| won't know without
asking the sailors, but...

00:12:11.994 --> 00:12:13.621
Can I count on you?

00:12:13.696 --> 00:12:14.788
Yeah...

00:12:14.864 --> 00:12:17.128
Get me a contact and I'll
make it worth your while.

00:12:17.199 --> 00:12:19.258
We'll be around
the port if you need us.

00:12:27.676 --> 00:12:29.940
Okay, on to the next tavern.

00:12:30.012 --> 00:12:33.141
Huh? Shouldn't
we just wait here?

00:12:33.215 --> 00:12:35.946
We need to spread the
word as far as possible.

00:12:36.018 --> 00:12:39.477
That'll increase our chances
of hooking somebody useful.

00:12:39.555 --> 00:12:41.785
You're something else, Ryna.

00:12:41.857 --> 00:12:45.088
Oh, you only just noticed that?

00:12:46.729 --> 00:12:50.222
You want to talk about
the Staff of Life, don't you?

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.399
Yes, Your Highness.

00:12:52.468 --> 00:12:54.493
The public doesn't know
about this...

00:12:54.570 --> 00:12:56.971
...but thieves broke into the
temple of Falis as well.

00:12:58.174 --> 00:12:59.505
Of course,

00:12:59.575 --> 00:13:03.705
the temple soldiers' strength
protected the Staff of Life.

00:13:03.779 --> 00:13:06.510
I see Lord Falis still holds this
land under his special protection.

00:13:06.582 --> 00:13:08.744
I'm relieved.

00:13:08.951 --> 00:13:12.080
I'm thankful for His providence.

00:13:12.154 --> 00:13:16.250
So, what will you,
the Doorway, do now?

00:13:16.325 --> 00:13:18.851
Now that I know the
Staff of Life is safe...

00:13:18.928 --> 00:13:21.022
...I can travel on
with peace of mind.

00:13:21.096 --> 00:13:23.121
To Marmo?

00:13:23.199 --> 00:13:27.227
If I do nothing, that dark
wizard will capture me one day.

00:13:27.303 --> 00:13:30.705
So I've decided to go there on my
own and try to settle things myself.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.975
And I want to recover
the Soul Crystal Ball...

00:13:34.043 --> 00:13:35.533
...for Master Spark's sake as well.

00:13:35.611 --> 00:13:38.342
As long as it remains
in Marmo hands,

00:13:38.414 --> 00:13:40.644
his heart will remain wounded.

00:13:41.217 --> 00:13:43.845
I know how it feels to want
to do things for others.

00:13:43.919 --> 00:13:48.186
But I also think you should
remember that you're just one girl.

00:13:50.059 --> 00:13:53.256
If anything happened to you, there
are people who'd be hurt by it.

00:13:53.329 --> 00:13:57.061
Your parents,
Wise Man Slayn and Leylia...

00:13:57.666 --> 00:13:59.828
That may be...

00:13:59.902 --> 00:14:03.270
But now I must be strong!

00:14:03.339 --> 00:14:07.071
If I'm not strong, my heart will
be enslaved by the Destroyer!

00:14:11.447 --> 00:14:14.109
I see there'll be
no changing your mind.

00:14:21.924 --> 00:14:25.588
May all the gods
of Light watch over you.

00:14:27.096 --> 00:14:30.157
Thank you very much, Highness...

00:14:48.784 --> 00:14:51.116
Thanks.

00:14:53.322 --> 00:14:56.019
Another miss.
That information we got was wrong.

00:14:56.091 --> 00:14:57.490
Oh, I see...

00:14:57.559 --> 00:15:02.224
Spark, it's sunset. I'm afraid we
have to get back to the castle.

00:15:08.504 --> 00:15:10.404
Sorry I wasn't much help.

00:15:10.472 --> 00:15:14.102
No, it's okay... I'm just sorry
you tried so hard on this.

00:15:17.012 --> 00:15:18.946
Well, don't let it get you down.

00:15:19.014 --> 00:15:21.039
We did everything we could...

00:15:21.116 --> 00:15:23.778
...50 let's take pride in
that and go back to Flaim.

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:30.850
All of you... Thank you.

00:15:30.926 --> 00:15:34.760
You guys! Are you the ones
looking for a ship to Kanon?

00:15:36.332 --> 00:15:38.164
Who are you?

00:15:38.233 --> 00:15:39.928
We don't have to tell you.

00:15:40.002 --> 00:15:42.061
Great! A smart-ass...

00:15:42.137 --> 00:15:44.799
Do you people really want to
become mercenaries for Marmo?

00:15:45.607 --> 00:15:47.803
Captain, these guys may be Marmo.

00:15:47.876 --> 00:15:48.843
Yeah, that's right!

00:15:48.911 --> 00:15:51.403
Thought so! None of
you are getting away!

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:54.040
Any friend of the Marmo
is an enemy of Valis!

00:15:54.116 --> 00:15:55.447
Uh-oh!

00:15:59.154 --> 00:16:00.451
What's going on?!

00:16:00.522 --> 00:16:02.456
These guys are Valis sailors!

00:16:02.524 --> 00:16:06.290
What do we do, Captain?
There's no backing out of this now!

00:16:06.362 --> 00:16:08.956
We can't fight and we can't
afford to be arrested.

00:16:09.031 --> 00:16:10.829
In this case, we run!

00:16:11.367 --> 00:16:12.835
I'll use my magic.

00:16:12.901 --> 00:16:15.097
Go to it, Aldo!

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:20.199
"Manna of all creation. Gentle
atmosphere which brings sleep..."

00:16:20.676 --> 00:16:25.580
"Let your power
enter their bodies..."

00:16:26.982 --> 00:16:28.643
"Fall into deep slumber!"

00:16:33.055 --> 00:16:35.547
Hurry! Now's our chance to run!

00:16:40.629 --> 00:16:42.290
Come back here!

00:16:51.774 --> 00:16:53.503
Garrack!

00:16:55.077 --> 00:16:56.135
I'm right here!

00:16:56.211 --> 00:16:57.144
Garrack...!

00:16:57.212 --> 00:16:59.613
I know what
you're thinking, Captain!

00:16:59.681 --> 00:17:02.844
Hold these jokers here till
the priest gets away, right?

00:17:05.888 --> 00:17:07.686
Let's show these
guys some real fighting!

00:17:07.756 --> 00:17:09.884
Just be careful
not to slice me up, too.

00:17:09.958 --> 00:17:11.653
I hear you!

00:17:14.463 --> 00:17:16.090
Forgive me, Priest!

00:17:17.866 --> 00:17:19.425
Uh, thank you.

00:17:28.277 --> 00:17:32.043
Captain, it's about
time we escaped, too.

00:17:32.114 --> 00:17:36.142
But there're so many of them we
couldn't run even if we wanted to!

00:17:43.158 --> 00:17:45.149
What the hell is that?!

00:17:51.767 --> 00:17:54.498
| summoned some will o' wisps.

00:17:54.570 --> 00:17:56.629
C'mon, if you're gonna run,
now's the time.

00:17:57.973 --> 00:17:59.873
We'll meet back in the city!

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:07.411
I hope they
all get away safely...

00:18:14.957 --> 00:18:16.447
In here.

00:18:17.626 --> 00:18:19.560
Stop!

00:18:35.644 --> 00:18:38.238
After them!
Don't let 'em get away!

00:18:41.884 --> 00:18:43.909
Thanks! That was close!

00:18:44.219 --> 00:18:47.519
That's all right. Taking on
a bunch of Valis sailors...

00:18:47.589 --> 00:18:49.318
You've got guts!

00:18:49.391 --> 00:18:51.416
It's not like |
wanted to fight them!

00:18:53.295 --> 00:18:55.559
So, what are you
going to do now?

00:18:55.631 --> 00:18:58.362
You can hide here
for a while if you want.

00:19:02.170 --> 00:19:05.196
No, I'm worried about my friends.
I'm going back to the city.

00:19:05.274 --> 00:19:07.572
You care about them.
I like that in a man.

00:19:07.643 --> 00:19:10.442
My name's Jay.
If you feel like it...

00:19:10.512 --> 00:19:12.844
...then come by the bridge
with your friends...

00:19:12.915 --> 00:19:14.815
...after the moon rises tonight.

00:19:16.652 --> 00:19:18.916
| can take you to Kanon.

00:19:20.722 --> 00:19:24.420
Let you become Marmo mercenaries,
just like you want to be.

00:19:43.645 --> 00:19:45.943
Welcome to Lodoss Island!

00:19:46.014 --> 00:19:48.813
And now, what you've been waiting
for, the second part of the show!

00:19:58.994 --> 00:20:01.827
Oh, I'm beat!

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:05.065
I'm really glad to finally
be out of that dungeon.

00:20:05.133 --> 00:20:07.966
But why did we wander in
there in the first place?!

00:20:08.036 --> 00:20:09.800
It may have been
the will of the gods.

00:20:09.871 --> 00:20:12.863
Oh, really? Hey, Neese!

00:20:12.941 --> 00:20:16.241
You can use magic to get
my strength back, can't you?

00:20:16.311 --> 00:20:18.336
- Yeah.
- Well, could you please?

00:20:18.413 --> 00:20:21.678
All right.
I'll give it a try.

00:20:21.750 --> 00:20:24.151
Great! I can't
stand being so weak!

00:20:24.386 --> 00:20:25.854
"Marfa, mother of the earth..."

00:20:25.921 --> 00:20:29.084
Something, something,
something, something...

00:20:29.157 --> 00:20:31.319
How did it go again...?

00:20:34.563 --> 00:20:36.053
Come on! Come on!

00:20:44.706 --> 00:20:47.539
Oh, dear. I made a mistake.

00:20:49.277 --> 00:20:50.802
What lively people you are.

00:20:50.879 --> 00:20:52.244
Oh! A priest!

00:20:52.414 --> 00:20:54.143
Travelers, eh? All right!

00:20:54.216 --> 00:20:58.050
I shall tell you some
especially good information.

00:20:58.120 --> 00:20:59.781
Thank you so much!

00:20:59.855 --> 00:21:02.950
Now then, my information is
"The Proper Way to Eat a Lollipop!"

00:21:04.192 --> 00:21:08.993
But, before I tell you, you have to
tell me something useful as well.

00:21:09.064 --> 00:21:11.726
And maybe give me
one of those..PLEASE?!

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:14.861
We can't! These are cookies
for the mama dragon!

00:21:18.607 --> 00:21:20.006
You're the Dark EIf!

00:21:20.075 --> 00:21:22.100
Oh, well.
The cat's out of the bag.

00:21:24.179 --> 00:21:25.169
He vanished!

00:21:25.247 --> 00:21:29.013
Well? You can't catch
me now, can you?

00:21:30.952 --> 00:21:34.286
Mark my words! I'll eat
your cookies eventually!

00:21:34.356 --> 00:21:36.256
He's, like, the total
opposite of a fearsome enemy.

00:21:36.324 --> 00:21:37.553
No kidding.

00:23:00.175 --> 00:23:03.110
A mysterious man appears
in the port of Roid.

00:23:03.178 --> 00:23:04.942
From what he tells us...

00:23:05.013 --> 00:23:08.244
...we believe that the holy
kingdom is about to be attacked.

00:23:08.316 --> 00:23:10.876
Are they aiming
for the temple of Falis?

00:23:10.952 --> 00:23:15.321
And what will Spark, who so longs
to be a knight, decide to do?

00:23:15.390 --> 00:23:18.690
Next time, on Record of Lodoss War -
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight:

00:23:18.760 --> 00:23:21.252
"Decision... An Option Compelled."
